 on what the user is asking for:\\n\\n1. `research` (default): full keyword metrics for a seed keyword plus related keyword suggestions. Use for global/topic research (\\\"research minecraft tips\\\", \\\"keyword ideas for cooking\\\"). Returns for each keyword:\\n   - Volume (0-100): How often people search for this keyword on YouTube\\n   - Competition (0-100): How many videos target this keyword\\n   - Overall score (0-100): Combined keyword opportunity score\\n   - Estimated monthly search volume, plus calibrated-baseline demand context when available\\n   - View momentum: recent daily views-per-hour data for the seed keyword, when available\\n   - Top markets: the countries where the keyword is most searched, with each country's share of searches\\n   - In-country volume: optionally pass a `country` (ISO 3166-1 alpha-2) to also get each keyword's estimated search volume within that country (the `countryVolume` field)\\n   Related keyword rows preserve the upstream relevance order and are capped at 20 suggestions.\\n\\n2. `questions`: question-style keyword searches matching a seed keyword, using the same indexed results and metrics as the vidIQ webapp. Requires `keyword`; use `language` to select the question-language index and `limit` to cap results. Set `sort='volume'` (default) for established demand or `sort='trending'` to preserve upstream raw-growth order. Treat `searchDemandGrowthPct` as a separate measured current-vs-baseline metric, not the server sort key; do not explain rows with null measured growth as sorted last by this tool. Results come back in `questions` with question, volume, competition, overall score, estimated monthly searches, normalized demand context, and raw upstream growth.\\n\\n3. `matching_terms`: precise long-tail keyword variations that preserve every normalized seed term, using the same Matching Terms path as the vidIQ webapp. Requires `keyword`; use `limit` to cap results. Set `sort='volume'` (default) for established demand or `sort='trending'` to preserve upstream raw-growth order. Treat `searchDemandGrowthPct` as a separate measured current-vs-baseline metric, not the server sort key; do not explain rows with null measured growth as sorted last by this tool. Results come back in `matchingTerms` with keyword, volume, competition, overall score, estimated monthly searches, calibrated 30-day baseline, metrics timestamp, normalized demand context, raw upstream growth, and trend baseline. Use this when the user asks for exact/long-tail variations of a phrase (e.g. \\\"matching terms for meal prep\\\" or \\\"long-tail variations of meal prep\\\"), not broad semantic ideas.\\n\\n4. `country_search`: the top keywords matching a TOPIC within ONE country and capped at `limit`. Use when the user names BOTH a topic AND a country — e.g. \\\"give me the top 10 minecraft keywords in IN\\\" → mode='country_search', keyword='minecraft', country='IN', limit=10. Requires `country` and `keyword`. Results come back in `relatedKeywords` (each row's `countryVolume` is the in-country volume; global YouTube metrics are null).\\n   - By default (`broad: false`) this is an EXACT/PHRASE match — every returned keyword literally contains the topic words (e.g. 'minecraft' → 'minecraft mods', 'minecraft house').\\n   - Set `broad: true` for a SEMANTIC match: the topic is first expanded into related keywords (the engine behind vidIQ's \\\"Related Keywords\\\" tab). Long-tail candidates preserving multiple meaningful seed terms rank before semantic-only candidates; within each tier, upstream related score then in-country volume determine order. The overlap boost is a lightweight heuristic: simple ASCII suffix matching applies only to ASCII Latin tokens, while other scripts require exact normalized token overlap. Country keyword text may be in any language; the `language` field only affects `questions` and `rising`. Returned keywords need NOT contain the topic words (e.g. 'minecraft' → 'redstone', 'survival mode'). Use this when the user wants a bigger/wider list, says \\\"related\\\"/\\\"similar\\\"/\\\"broaden\\\", or the exact-match list is too small.\\n\\n5. `country_top`: the top keywords overall within ONE country (NO topic filter), ranked by in-country search volume and capped at `limit`. Use when the user names a country but no topic, e.g. \\\"what are the top keywords in Brazil\\\" → mode='country_top', country='BR'. Requires `country`; `keyword` is ignored. Results come back in `relatedKeywords` as above.\\n\\n6. `rising`: keywords gaining search momentum over time, like the vidIQ dashboard's \\\"Rising Keywords\\\" tab. Use when the user asks for rising, trending, or gaining-momentum keywords. Choose the trend window with `period`. Optionally scope to a category with `topic` — this MUST be one of the values in the response's `availableTopics` (call 'rising' with no `topic` first to discover them; passing an unknown topic returns an error listing the valid ones). Omit `topic` for overall trends, in which case `availableTopics` lists every category you can drill into. This returns keyword METRICS with growth, not videos. Results come back in `risingKeywords`, not `relatedKeywords`.\\n\\nCost: 5 credit(s) per call.\",\"parameters\":{\"$schema\":\"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\",\"properties\":{\"broad\":{\"default\":false,\"description\":\"Only applies to 'country_search' mode. Controls how the topic is matched within the country:\\n- false (default) = EXACT/PHRASE match: returns only keywords whose text actually contains the topic words. E.g. topic 'minecraft' returns 'minecraft', 'minecraft mods', 'minecraft house'; every result literally contains 'minecraft'. Use when the user wants variants of a specific phrase.\\n- true = SEMANTIC/BROAD match: first expands the topic into related keywords (the same engine behind vidIQ's 'Related Keywords' tab). For long-tail seeds, candidates preserving multiple meaningful seed terms rank before semantic-only candidates; within each tier, upstream related score then in-country volume determine order. This is a lightweight overlap heuristic, not language detection: simple ASCII suffix matching applies only to ASCII Latin tokens, while other scripts require exact normalized token overlap. Results need NOT contain the topic words, so a short topic such as 'minecraft' can still return 'redstone', 'survival mode', and 'building ideas'. Use when the user wants a BIGGER / wider list of related ideas, says 'related', 'similar', 'broaden', 'more than just X', or complains the exact-match list is too small.\",\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"country\":{\"description\":\"ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 country code (for example 'US', 'IN'). In 'research' mode this is optional and enriches each keyword with its estimated in-country search volume (the `countryVolume` field). REQUIRED for 'country_top' and 'country_search' modes. Not supported in 'rising' mode.\",\"maxLength\":2,\"minLength\":2,\"type\":\"string\"},\"includeRelated\":{\"default\":true,\"description\":\"Include related keyword suggestions ('research' mode only)\",\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"keyword\":{\"description\":\"Seed keyword / topic (for example 'minecraft tips'). Required for 'research', 'questions', 'matching_terms', and 'country_search'; ignored for 'country_top'; not used in 'rising' (use `topic` to scope rising trends).\",\"maxLength\":150,\"minLength\":1,\"type\":\"string\"},\"language\":{\"default\":\"en\",\"description\":\"Language for 'questions' or 'rising' mode (case-insensitive). Questions supports any, en, es, pt, ru, sv. Rising supports all, en, ru, es, pt. Defaults to en. This field does not constrain research or country searches.\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"limit\":{\"default\":20,\"description\":\"Maximum number of results to return for 'questions', 'matching_terms', 'country_top', 'country_search', and 'rising' modes. Ignored in 'research' mode.\",\"maximum\":100,\"minimum\":1,\"type\":\"integer\"},\"mode\":{\"default\":\"research\",\"description\":\"Which kind of keyword research to run. Pick based on the user's question:\\n- 'research' (default): full metrics for a seed keyword plus recent daily views-per-hour momentum and related keyword suggestions. Demand context distinguishes unknown, below-threshold (\\u003c750), and measurable monthly searches, with baseline, normalized growth, freshness, and webapp-aligned volume bands when upstream data exists. Optionally pass `country` to enrich every row with in-country search volume.\\n- 'questions': indexed question-style searches matching a seed keyword, with the same normalized demand context plus volume, competition, and opportunity. Use `sort: 'volume'` for established demand or `sort: 'trending'` to preserve upstream raw-growth order. Treat `searchDemandGrowthPct` as a separate measured current-vs-baseline metric, not the server sort key; do not say null measured-growth rows were sorted last unless the upstream response itself proves that ordering. Requires `keyword`; `language` controls the question-language index.\\n- 'matching_terms': precise long-tail keyword variations that preserve every normalized seed term, with the same normalized demand context plus the raw upstream growth/trend-baseline fields for compatibility. Use for exact phrase variants like 'long-tail variations of meal prep'. Requires `keyword`; use `sort: 'volume'` for established demand or `sort: 'trending'` to preserve upstream raw-growth order. Treat `searchDemandGrowthPct` as a separate measured current-vs-baseline metric, not the server sort key; do not say null measured-growth rows were sorted last unless the upstream response itself proves that ordering.\\n- 'country_search': the top keywords matching a topic WITHIN one country. By default, exact/phrase matches are ranked by in-country volume. With `broad: true`, long-tail matches preserving meaningful seed terms rank before semantic-only discoveries; within each tier, upstream related score and in-country volume determine order. Requires `country` and `keyword`.\\n- 'country_top': the top keywords overall within one country, ranked by in-country search volume, with NO topic filter. Use when the user names a country but no topic, e.g. 'what are the top keywords in Brazil'. Requires `country`; `keyword` is ignored.\\n- 'rising': keywords gaining search momentum globally over a day, week, or month. Optionally scope to a category via `topic` (a value from `availableTopics`); omit `topic` for overall trends plus the discoverable topic list. Results include growth metrics in `risingKeywords`.\",\"enum\":[\"research\",\"questions\",\"matching_terms\",\"country_top\",\"country_search\",\"rising\"],\"type\":\"string\"},\"period\":{\"default\":\"week\",\"description\":\"Trend window for 'rising' mode. Only meaningful in 'rising' mode.\",\"enum\":[\"day\",\"week\",\"month\"],\"type\":\"string\"},\"sort\":{\"default\":\"volume\",\"description\":\"Ranking for 'questions' and 'matching_terms' modes: 'volume' (default) ranks by search volume; 'trending' preserves upstream raw-growth order. Do not assume 'trending' is sorted by normalized searchDemandGrowthPct, and do not explain null searchDemandGrowthPct rows as locally sorted last. Ignored in other modes.\",\"enum\":[\"volume\",\"trending\"],\"type\":\"string\"},\"topic\":{\"description\":\"Category to scope 'rising' results to (for example \\\"trailers\\\", when listed in `availableTopics`). Must be one of the values returned in `availableTopics` for the requested period — call 'rising' without a `topic` first to discover them. Matching is case-insensitive. Omit for overall (non-topic-scoped) rising trends. Ignored outside 'rising' mode; use `keyword` for the research seed.\",\"minLength\":1,\"type\":\"string\"}},\"type\":\"object\"}}\nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n"}
{"step_index":18,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-14T09:17:50Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-14T14:47:50+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-09-14T14:47:50+05:30\nFile Path: `file:///C:/Users/renu5/.gemini/antigravity/mcp/vidiq/vidiq_channel_search.json`\nTotal Lines: 1\nTotal Bytes: 20889\nShowing lines 1 to 1\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: {\"name\":\"vidiq_channel_search\",\"description\":\"Comprehensive YouTube channel search. Combines semantic + lexical text search with structured filters across identity, audience size, growth, format mix, and content metadata.\\n\\nUse this tool to:\\n- Find channels by niche or topic with natural-language queries (semantic match on niche + description embeddings).\\n- Look up a specific channel by YouTube handle (e.g. '@MrBeast').\\n- Require specific wording in the channel description with the description filter (consecutive words, typo-tolerant) — for 'channels whose description mentions/says X'.\\n- Filter by channel size (subscriber/view/video count ranges), growth (7d / 30d / 1y subs and views), recency (last video published), format (long / short / mixed), per-format average duration and video/view counts (7d / 30d / 1y), creation date, country, language, main category, and flags (faceless, breakout).\\n- Order results with the optional sort param (relevance / subscriberCount / subsGrowth30d / viewsGrowth30d / lastVideoPublished). Topical asks — including 'top/popular/biggest channels about X' — use relevance (default), which already favors notable channels; field sorts are ONLY for explicit metric scans and re-order by the raw metric, ignoring topical fit.\\n- Combine any subset of inputs — at least one of query / handle / channel title / filters is required.\\n- Find emerging channels: set breakoutChannel: true for any 'breakout / emerging / up-and-coming channels in X' intent — the flag filters to breakout channels AND switches ranking to favor small fast-rising channels (replaces vidiq_breakout_channels).\\n- Non-English / local discovery: `languages` means the actual language channels publish in; `country` means where channels are based, not audience location or content language. Never translate the query — 'дай каналы про уроки макияжа' → query: 'уроки макияжа', languages: ['ru']; 'tokyo street food' → query: 'tokyo street food', country: ['JP']; 'news and politics in Ukraine' → country: ['UA'] (news/politics/local-events about a country means that country's channels, not foreign coverage). Results should match the request's language unless the user says otherwise. For geo-local or language-specific discovery request limit 20+ — relevant local channels may rank below globally popular ones.\\n\\nFor finding COMPETITORS of a channel — the user's own (\\\"who are my competitors?\\\") or a named one (\\\"channels similar to Creator Insider\\\") — prefer vidiq_similar_channels (auto-exclusion and competitor-tuned scoring); this tool is still the right first step there, to resolve the reference channel's niche, subNiches, subscriberCount, country, and languages. For viral-video discovery, use vidiq_outliers.\\n\\nCost: 5 credit(s) per call.\",\"parameters\":{\"$schema\":\"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\",\"properties\":{\"avgViewsMax\":{\"description\":\"Maximum lifetime average views per video (total views / total videos). Use for 'averages under 10k views a video'.\",\"minimum\":0,\"type\":\"number\"},\"avgViewsMin\":{\"description\":\"Minimum lifetime average views per video (total views / total videos). Use for 'averages 100k+ views per video'. This is the per-video average, not total views.\",\"minimum\":0,\"type\":\"number\"},\"breakoutChannel\":{\"description\":\"Filter by breakout-channel flag. true also switches ranking to emerging-channel mode: the popularity prior is disabled so small fast-rising channels rank by pure relevance instead of being outranked by established ones. Use breakoutChannel: true for any 'breakout / emerging / up-and-coming channels in X' intent. Omit to return both breakout and non-breakout channels with default ranking.\",\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"channelTitle\":{\"description\":\"Optional channel title fragment to bias results toward channels whose title matches (e.g. 'Mark Rober').\",\"maxLength\":200,\"minLength\":1,\"type\":\"string\"},\"channelTitleMatch\":{\"description\":\"How to match channelTitle. 'fuzzy' (default) ranks by title similarity (partial matches allowed). 'exact' restricts to channels whose title equals the value (case-insensitive). Requires channelTitle — rejected if set without it.\",\"enum\":[\"exact\",\"fuzzy\"],\"type\":\"string\"},\"channelType\":{\"description\":\"Filter by content format: 'long' (longform), 'short' (shorts-first), or 'mixed'.\",\"enum\":[\"long\",\"short\",\"mixed\"],\"type\":\"string\"},\"country\":{\"description\":\"Filter by channel country (ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 codes, uppercase, e.g. ['US', 'GB']): the country where the channel is BASED — NOT the audience/viewer country, and NOT the channel's language (use `languages` to filter by language). Multiple codes are OR-ed. When the query names a place ('tokyo street food', 'nyc daily vlogs'), pass the corresponding country code(s) — e.g. tokyo → ['JP'] — and keep the city name in the query. For news, politics, or local-events queries about a country ('news and politics in Ukraine'), ALWAYS set that country (usually with its language in `languages`): the audience wants that country's channels, not foreign channels covering it. Skip the country filter only for travel/culture coverage intent where creators from anywhere qualify ('travel vlogs about Japan').\",\"items\":{\"maxLength\":2,\"minLength\":2,\"type\":\"string\"},\"maxItems\":20,\"minItems\":1,\"type\":\"array\"},\"description\":{\"description\":\"Require a phrase in the channel description: the words must appear consecutively, in order, each tolerating small typos. A hard filter (restricts the result set, works with any sort), unlike `query` which only ranks. Use when the user wants channels whose DESCRIPTION says something specific (e.g. description: 'redstone tutorials' or 'business inquiries'). For topic/niche discovery, prefer `query`.\",\"maxLength\":500,\"minLength\":1,\"type\":\"string\"},\"estimatedEarningsMax\":{\"description\":\"Maximum estimated MONTHLY channel earnings in USD. Hard filter: channels with unknown earnings are excluded. Use for 'channels making under $1000 a month'.\",\"minimum\":0,\"type\":\"number\"},\"estimatedEarningsMin\":{\"description\":\"Minimum estimated MONTHLY channel earnings in USD. Hard filter: channels with unknown earnings are excluded. Use for 'channels earning over $10k a month'.\",\"minimum\":0,\"type\":\"number\"},\"exactLanguage\":{\"description\":\"When true, match languages exactly (only monolingual channels whose single language equals the requested code). Prefer true when the user wants content purely in that language — multilingual channels (e.g. 'hi, en') often produce content mostly in their other language. When false/omitted, match any channel containing the requested language(s). Requires a non-empty `languages` list — rejected if true without it.\",\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"faceless\":{\"description\":\"Filter by faceless-channel status. true returns only faceless channels, false excludes them.\",\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"handle\":{\"description\":\"YouTube handle / custom URL (e.g. '@MrBeast' or 'mrbeast'). Leading '@' is optional. Use this when you want a specific channel.\",\"maxLength\":100,\"minLength\":1,\"type\":\"string\"},\"handleMatch\":{\"description\":\"How to match handle. 'exact' (default) returns only the channel with that exact handle. 'fuzzy' does a partial/relevance match (e.g. 'beast' matches '@MrBeast'). Requires handle — rejected if set without it.\",\"enum\":[\"exact\",\"fuzzy\"],\"type\":\"string\"},\"languages\":{\"description\":\"Filter by the actual language(s) the channels publish content in (ISO 639-1 codes, lowercase, e.g. ['en', 'es']). Always pass the user's requested content/channel language here; this is channel language, NOT channel country. When the USER'S REQUEST is written in a non-English language and does not request a different content language, or they explicitly ask for content in a specific language ('на русском', 'auf deutsch'), pass that actual content language here — e.g. query 'уроки макияжа' → languages: ['ru']. Do not translate the query; the search understands non-English text, but without this filter big channels in other languages will outrank local ones. By default matches any channel that *contains* a requested language (multilingual channels included). Set exactLanguage=true to return only monolingual channels whose language is exactly the requested value.\",\"items\":{\"pattern\":\"^[A-Za-z]{2}$\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"maxItems\":20,\"minItems\":1,\"type\":\"array\"},\"lastVideoPublishedAfter\":{\"description\":\"Last uploaded video on or after this date (ISO YYYY-MM-DD) — active channels.\",\"format\":\"date\",\"pattern\":\"^(?:(?:\\\\d\\\\d[2468][048]|\\\\d\\\\d[13579][26]|\\\\d\\\\d0[48]|[02468][048]00|[13579][26]00)-02-29|\\\\d{4}-(?:(?:0[13578]|1[02])-(?:0[1-9]|[12]\\\\d|3[01])|(?:0[469]|11)-(?:0[1-9]|[12]\\\\d|30)|(?:02)-(?:0[1-9]|1\\\\d|2[0-8])))$\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"lastVideoPublishedBefore\":{\"description\":\"Last uploaded video on or before this date (ISO YYYY-MM-DD).\",\"format\":\"date\",\"pattern\":\"^(?:(?:\\\\d\\\\d[2468][048]|\\\\d\\\\d[13579][26]|\\\\d\\\\d0[48]|[02468][048]00|[13579][26]00)-02-29|\\\\d{4}-(?:(?:0[13578]|1[02])-(?:0[1-9]|[12]\\\\d|3[01])|(?:0[469]|11)-(?:0[1-9]|[12]\\\\d|30)|(?:02)-(?:0[1-9]|1\\\\d|2[0-8])))$\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"limit\":{\"default\":10,\"description\":\"Number of channels to return (max 50). For geo-local or language-specific discovery, request 20+ — relevant local channels may rank below globally popular ones.\",\"maximum\":50,\"minimum\":1,\"type\":\"integer\"},\"longAvgDuration1yMax\":{\"description\":\"Maximum average long-form video duration over the trailing year (seconds).\",\"minimum\":0,\"type\":\"number\"},\"longAvgDuration1yMin\":{\"description\":\"Minimum average long-form video duration over the trailing year (seconds).\",\"minimum\":0,\"type\":\"number\"},\"longAvgDuration30dMax\":{\"description\":\"Maximum average long-form video duration over the trailing 30 days (seconds).\",\"minimum\":0,\"type\":\"number\"},\"longAvgDuration30dMin\":{\"description\":\"Minimum average long-form video duration over the trailing 30 days (seconds).\",\"minimum\":0,\"type\":\"number\"},\"longAvgDuration7dMax\":{\"description\":\"Maximum average long-form video duration over the trailing 7 days (seconds).\",\"minimum\":0,\"type\":\"number\"},\"longAvgDuration7dMin\":{\"description\":\"Minimum average long-form video duration over the trailing 7 days (seconds).\",\"minimum\":0,\"type\":\"number\"},\"longVideoCount1yMax\":{\"description\":\"Maximum number of long-form videos published in the trailing year.\",\"maximum\":9007199254740991,\"minimum\":0,\"type\":\"integer\"},\"longVideoCount1yMin\":{\"description\":\"Minimum number of long-form videos published in the trailing year.\",\"maximum\":9007199254740991,\"minimum\":0,\"type\":\"integer\"},\"longVideoCount30dMax\":{\"description\":\"Maximum number of long-form videos published in the trailing 30 days.\",\"maximum\":9007199254740991,\"minimum\":0,\"type\":\"integer\"},\"longVideoCount30dMin\":{\"description\":\"Minimum number of long-form videos published in the trailing 30 days.\",\"maximum\":9007199254740991,\"minimum\":0,\"type\":\"integer\"},\"longVideoCount7dMax\":{\"description\":\"Maximum number of long-form videos published in the trailing 7 days.\",\"maximum\":9007199254740991,\"minimum\":0,\"type\":\"integer\"},\"longVideoCount7dMin\":{\"description\":\"Minimum number of long-form videos published in the trailing 7 days.\",\"maximum\":9007199254740991,\"minimum\":0,\"type\":\"integer\"},\"longViewCount1yMax\":{\"description\":\"Maximum long-form view count accrued in the trailing year.\",\"maximum\":9007199254740991,\"minimum\":0,\"type\":\"integer\"},\"longViewCount1yMin\":{\"description\":\"Minimum long-form view count accrued in the trailing year.\",\"maximum\":9007199254740991,\"minimum\":0,\"type\":\"integer\"},\"longViewCount30dMax\":{\"description\":\"Maximum long-form view count accrued in the trailing 30 days.\",\"maximum\":9007199254740991,\"minimum\":0,\"type\":\"integer\"},\"longViewCount30dMin\":{\"description\":\"Minimum long-form view count accrued in the trailing 30 days.\",\"maximum\":9007199254740991,\"minimum\":0,\"type\":\"integer\"},\"longViewCount7dMax\":{\"description\":\"Maximum long-form view count accrued in the trailing 7 days.\",\"maximum\":9007199254740991,\"minimum\":0,\"type\":\"integer\"},\"longViewCount7dMin\":{\"description\":\"Minimum long-form view count accrued in the trailing 7 days.\",\"maximum\":9007199254740991,\"minimum\":0,\"type\":\"integer\"},\"mainCategory\":{\"description\":\"Filter by main category (YouTube topic labels as stored in the index — e.g. 'Knowledge' for educational content, 'Video game culture' for gaming, 'Lifestyle (sociology)' for lifestyle). Values are case-sensitive and must come from the enum; multiple values are OR-ed.\",\"items\":{\"enum\":[\"Music\",\"Christian music\",\"Classical music\",\"Country music\",\"Electronic music\",\"Hip hop music\",\"Independent music\",\"Jazz\",\"Music of Asia\",\"Music of Latin America\",\"Pop music\",\"Reggae\",\"Rhythm and blues\",\"Rock music\",\"Soul music\",\"Video game culture\",\"Action game\",\"Action-adventure game\",\"Casual game\",\"Music video game\",\"Puzzle video game\",\"Racing video game\",\"Role-playing video g